Setting up the environment:

You can use my docker:
sudo docker run --gpus all -it --rm --net=host --privileged -v /tmp/.X11-unix:/tmp/.X11-unix -e DISPLAY=$DISPLAY --mount type=bind,src=/home/colin/Deepstream/DeepstreamSolution,dst=/DeepstreamSolution deepstreamsolutiondocker


1) Running the nvidia deepstream docker. 

Before running the nvidia docker, you'll need to install NVIDIA Container Toolkit. 
Refer to this page: https://docs.nvidia.com/datacenter/cloud-native/container-toolkit/install-guide.html#docker

Then run the following commands:

xhost +
sudo docker run --gpus all -it --rm --net=host --privileged -v /tmp/.X11-unix:/tmp/.X11-unix -e DISPLAY=$DISPLAY --mount type=bind,src=/home/colin/Deepstream/DeepstreamSolution,dst=/DeepstreamSolution -w /opt/nvidia/deepstream/deepstream-6.1 nvcr.io/nvidia/deepstream:6.1.1-devel


2) To get additional modules (like avenc_mpeg4 encoder) install the user_additional_install:

./user_additional_install.sh

3) Install the DeepStream python bindings (https://github.com/NVIDIA-AI-IOT/deepstream_python_apps/tree/master/bindings):

Base dependencies:

apt install python3-gi python3-dev python3-gst-1.0 python-gi-dev git python-dev \
    python3 python3-pip python3.8-dev cmake g++ build-essential libglib2.0-dev \
    libglib2.0-dev-bin libgstreamer1.0-dev libtool m4 autoconf automake libgirepository1.0-dev libcairo2-dev

clone the deepstream_python_apps(https://github.com/NVIDIA-AI-IOT/deepstream_python_apps):

cd sources
git clone https://github.com/NVIDIA-AI-IOT/deepstream_python_apps.git

# since we're using deepstream 6.1, we'll checkout an earlier version 
cd deepstream_python_apps/
git checkout v1.1.4

Initialization of submodules:
cd /opt/nvidia/deepstream/deepstream/sources/deepstream_python_apps/
git submodule update --init

Installing Gst-python: 
sudo apt-get install -y apt-transport-https ca-certificates -y
sudo update-ca-certificates
cd 3rdparty/gst-python/
./autogen.sh
make
sudo make install

Compiling the bindings:
cd deepstream_python_apps/bindings
mkdir build
cd build
cmake ..
make

Installing the bindings:
pip3 install ./pyds-1.1.4-py3-none*.whl

3) Installing other dependencies needed in the code:

pip install pika jsonlib-python3 protobuf opencv-python mysql-connector-python


4) Setup mysql (https://phoenixnap.com/kb/install-mysql-ubuntu-20-04)

Step 1: Update/Upgrade Package Repository
sudo apt update
sudo apt upgrade

Step 2: Install MySQL
sudo apt install mysql-server
mysql --version

Step 3: Securing MySQL
sudo mysql_secure_installation
- enter and renter password (we use Password)

Step 4: Check if MySQL Service Is Running
sudo systemctl status mysql

Step 5: Log in to MySQL Server
sudo mysql -u root


